<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Basutoland National Council</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1903–1965</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Basutoland National Council was a body of chiefs and nominated members created in 1903 to advise the British administration of Basutoland, presided over by the Paramount Chief. It gave chiefs a formal voice in colonial government. Reforms in 1960 added elected members and legislative powers, preparing the way for Lesotho's independence in 1966.</p></div>
